hadiths[256]{hadithnumber,text}:
"919","Ibn Abbas reported that the delegation of Abdul Qais came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! We are this tribe from Rabi'ah, and the disbelievers of Mudar have come between us and you, so we cannot reach you except in the sacred month. So command us with a command that we can act upon and invite those behind us to it."" He said: ""I command you with four things and forbid you from four things: Faith in Allah."" Then he explained it to them, saying: ""Testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakah, and that you give one-fifth of what you gain as booty."" And he forbade you from dubba, hantam, naqir, and muqayyar."
"920","[AI-translation] Khuza'i who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, came out to us and said: Give glad tidings, give glad tidings! Do you not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? They said: Yes. He said: Then this Quran is a rope, one end of which is in the hand of Allah and the other end is in your hands. So hold fast to it, for you will never go astray nor perish after it ever."
"921","[AI-translation] From Abu Bakr ibn Abu Musa from his father who said: I came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and with me was a group of my people. He said: Give glad tidings, and give glad tidings to those behind you, for whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah truthfully will enter Paradise. So we left the Prophet, peace be upon him, to give glad tidings to the people. Umar ibn al-Khattab met us and took us back to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him. The Messenger of Allah said: Who turned you back? They said: Umar. He said: Why did you turn them back, O Umar? Umar said: Then the people will rely on it. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, remained silent."
"922","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: The most hateful of people to Allah are three: a deviant in the Sanctuary, one who seeks in Islam the way of the Jahiliyyah, and one who seeks to shed the blood of a person without right."
"923","On the authority of Qutaylah bint Sayfiyy al-Juhaniyyah, she said: A scholar from the scholars came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: ""O Muhammad! What excellent people you are, were it not that you associate partners (with Allah)."" He said: ""Glory be to Allah! And what is that?"" He said: ""You say when you swear: 'By the Ka'bah.'"" She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) paused for a while, then said: ""Indeed it has been revealed: 'So whoever swears, let him swear by the Lord of the Ka'bah.'"" He said: ""O Muhammad! What excellent people you are, were it not that you make for Allah a rival."" He said: ""Glory be to Allah! And what is that?"" He said: ""You say: 'What Allah wills and you will.'"" She said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) paused for a while, then said: ""Indeed it has been revealed: 'So whoever says ""What Allah wills,"" let him say with it: ""Then you will.""'"""
"924","[AI-translation] From Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: Avoid the major sins, be steadfast, and give glad tidings."
"925","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas who said: A man came to the Prophet and disputed with him concerning some words, and said: ""What Allah willed and you willed."" The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said to him: ""Have you made me an equal to Allah?"" - in a wording: a peer - ""No, rather, what Allah alone willed."
"926","[AI-translation] From Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Record for me everyone who has professed Islam."" He said: We said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Do you fear for us when we are between six hundred and seven hundred?"" So the Messenger of Allah said: ""You do not know; perhaps you will be tested."" He said: So we were tested until a man among us would not pray except in secret."
"927","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, raised to the Prophet: Swear by Allah and be righteous and speak the truth, for Allah hates that one swears by anything other than Him."
"928","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, was asked which religions are most beloved to Allah. He said: The tolerant Hanifiyyah."
"929","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: Delving into Qadar is deferred for the worst of my Ummah at the end of time."
"930","[AI-translation] From Sulaym ibn Amir who said: I heard Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Go out and announce to the people: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah, Paradise is guaranteed for him."" He said: So I went out, and Umar ibn al-Khattab met me and said: ""What is the matter with you, O Abu Bakr?"" I said: ""The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said to me: Go out and announce to the people: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah, Paradise is guaranteed for him."" Umar said: ""Return to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, for I fear they will rely upon it."" So I returned to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and he said: ""What brought you back?"" So I informed him of what Umar said, and he said: ""He spoke the truth."
"931","[AI-translation] Hujaymi, from a man from Bahlhujaym who said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, to what do you call?"" He said: ""I call to Allah alone, the One who, if harm touches you and you supplicate to Him, He lifts it from you; the One who, if you become lost in a barren land and you supplicate to Him, He returns you; and the One who, if a year of drought strikes you and you supplicate to Him, He causes growth for you."
"932","Abu Burdah narrated from his father (Abu Musa al-Ash'ari) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) sent me and Mu'adh to Yemen, and he said: ""Call the people, give glad tidings, and do not cause aversion; make things easy, and do not make things difficult."" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Give us a ruling concerning two drinks which we used to prepare in Yemen: Al-Bit', which is made from honey and is fermented until it becomes strong; and Al-Mizr, which is made from millet and is fermented until it becomes strong."" He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) had been given comprehensive words with their conclusive meanings, so he said: ""I prohibit every intoxicant that prevents (one) from prayer."" And in a narration of Muslim (6/99): ""And teach (them)"" instead of ""and do not make things difficult."""
"933","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, from Muhammad the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him: When one of you perfects his Islam, every good deed he performs is recorded as tenfold up to seven hundred times, and every evil deed he performs is recorded for him as its equal, until he meets Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"934","[AI-translation] Hudhali said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: When Allah intends to seize a servant in a land, He makes for him a need in it. ( )"
"935","[AI-translation] Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: When a servant embraces Islam and his Islam is good, Allah records for him every good deed he had done, and erases from him every evil deed he had done. Then after that is the reckoning: the good deed is ten times its like up to seven hundredfold, and the evil deed is by its like, unless Allah, Mighty and Majestic, pardons it."
"936","[AI-translation] Abdullah said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: When Allah speaks with the revelation, the dwellers of the heaven hear a clanking for the heaven like the dragging of a chain over the solid rock, and they swoon. They remain in that state until Jibril comes to them. When Jibril comes, fear is removed from their hearts. He said: They say, ""O Jibril, what did your Lord say?"" He says, ""The truth."" They say, ""The truth, the truth."
"937","[AI-translation] Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: When one of you swears, let him not say, ""What Allah willed and you willed,"" but let him say, ""What Allah willed, then you willed."
"938","[AI-translation] Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: When a servant commits adultery, faith departs from him and is like a canopy. When he withdraws from it, faith returns to him."
"939","[AI-translation] Abu Umamah said: A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah, what is faith?"" He said: ""When your good deed pleases you and your evil deed grieves you, then you are a believer."" He said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What is sin?"" He said: ""When something causes unease in your chest, leave it."
"940","[AI-translation] Abdullah said: A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! How will I know if I have done good?"" He said: ""If you hear your neighbors say, 'You have done good,' then you have done good. And if you hear them say, 'You have done bad,' then you have done bad."
"941","[AI-translation] From Imran bin Husayn from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, he said: When a man says to his brother, ""O disbeliever,"" it is like killing him. And cursing a believer is like killing him."
"942","Abu Hurairah said: We were sitting around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with Abu Bakr and Umar among a group of people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up from among us and was delayed, so we feared he might be cut off from us. We were alarmed and stood up, and I was the first to be alarmed. I went out seeking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until I came to a wall belonging to the Ansar of Banu al-Najjar. I circled it looking for a door but found none. Then I saw a water channel entering through the hollow of the wall from a well outside—and the rabī' is the water channel. So I clambered up and entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: ""Abu Hurairah?"" I said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""What is the matter with you?"" I said: ""You were among us, then you stood up and were delayed, so we feared you might be cut off from us. We were alarmed, and I was the first to be alarmed. I came to this wall and clambered up as a fox clambers, and these people are behind me."" He said: ""O Abu Hurairah!"" And he gave me his two sandals. He said: ""Go with these two sandals of mine. Whomever you meet behind this wall who testifies that there is no god but Allah, with his heart certain of it, give him glad tidings of Paradise.""The first one I met was Umar. He said: ""What are these two sandals, O Abu Hurairah?"" I said: ""These are the sandals of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He sent me with them: whomever I meet who testifies that there is no god but Allah, with his heart certain of it, I give him glad tidings of Paradise."" Umar struck his hand between my breasts, and I fell on my backside. He said: ""Return, O Abu Hurairah."" So I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ weeping bitterly, and Umar was following behind me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""What is the matter with you, O Abu Hurairah?"" I said: ""I met Umar and informed him of what you sent me with. He struck between my breasts a blow that made me fall on my backside, and said: 'Return.'"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""O Umar! What prompted you to do what you did?"" He said: ""O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransomed for you. Did you send Abu Hurairah with your sandals that whomever he meets who testifies that there is no god but Allah, with his heart certain of it, he gives him glad tidings of Paradise?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Then do not do it, for I fear that people will rely upon it. Leave them to do deeds."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Leave them."""
"943","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: Four things in my nation from the affairs of the Days of Ignorance the people will not abandon: wailing, impugning lineages, contagion—a mangy camel infected a hundred camels, who infected the first camel?—and the stars, ""We were given rain by such and such star."
"944","[AI-translation] Ash'ari, raised to the Prophet: Four things in my nation from the affairs of the Days of Ignorance they will not abandon: boasting of lineages, impugning ancestors, seeking rain through the stars, and wailing."
"945","On the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Sari', attributed to the Prophet: Four people will present an argument on the Day of Resurrection: a deaf man who cannot hear, a fool, a senile old man, and one who died during the interval (between prophets). As for the deaf man, he will say: ""O Lord, Islam came but I heard nothing."" As for the fool, he will say: ""Islam came and the children were pelting me with dung."" As for the senile old man, he will say: ""Islam came but I could not understand."" As for the one who died during the interval, he will say: ""O Lord! No messenger of Yours came to me."" Then He will take their covenants to obey Him, and He will send a messenger to them saying: ""Enter the Fire."" He (the Prophet) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if they entered it, it would have been coolness and peace for them."""
"946","[AI-translation] From Anas that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said to a man: Embrace Islam. He said: I find myself averse. He said: Embrace Islam even if you are averse."
"947","[AI-translation] From Hakim bin Hizam, elevated to the Prophet: You have embraced Islam upon whatever good you have already done."
"948","Narrated by ʿUmar, who said: We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a military expedition. We said: ""O Messenger of Allah, the enemy has drawn near and they are well-fed while the people are hungry."" The Anṣār said: ""Shall we not slaughter our camels and feed them to the people?"" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Whoever has surplus food, let him bring it."" So they began bringing a mudd, a ṣāʿ, more and less. The total of what was in the army amounted to twenty-some ṣāʿs. The Prophet ﷺ sat beside it and invoked blessing. The Prophet ﷺ said: ""Take, but do not be greedy."" So a man would take in his sack and his bag, and they took in their vessels, until a man would tie the sleeve of his shirt and fill it. They finished and the food remained as it was. Then the Prophet ﷺ said: ""I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah. No servant meets Allah with these two [testimonies], being sincere in them, except that Allah will protect him from the Fire."""
"949","[AI-translation] Darda', when death approached him, he said: Shall I narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family? I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: Worship Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, indeed He sees you. Count yourself among the dead. Beware of the supplication of the oppressed, for it is answered. And whoever among you is able to attend the two prayers, Al-Isha and Al-Fajr, even if crawling, let him do so."
"950","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, took hold of a part of my body and said: Worship Allah as if you see Him, and be in the world as if you are a stranger or a wayfarer."
"951","[AI-translation] From Mu'adh, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, instruct me. He said: Worship Allah as if you see Him, and count yourself among the dead. Remember Allah near every stone and every tree. And if you do an evil deed, do a good deed next to it; the secret for the secret, and the public for the public."
"952","On the authority of Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from a man, from a companion of his, from his father — and his father was known as Abu al-Muntafiq — who said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ at Arafat, and I drew near to him until the neck of my mount touched the neck of his mount. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, inform me of a deed that will save me from Allah's punishment and admit me into His Paradise."" He said: ""Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prescribed prayer, pay the obligatory zakat, perform Hajj and Umrah."" He said: ""I bear witness,"" and I think he said: ""And fast Ramadan. And consider what you love for people to do to you, so do it to them; and what you dislike from people doing to you, so leave them from it."""
"953","[AI-translation] Thaqafi, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother bequeathed to me to free a slave on her behalf, and I have a black Nubian slave girl. He, peace be upon him, said: Call her. He said: Who is your Lord? She said: Allah. He said: Who am I? She said: The Messenger of Allah. He said: Free her, for she is a believer."
"954","[AI-translation] From Ma'qal bin Yasar, elevated: The best of faith is patience and forbearance."
"955","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr, elevated: The best of deeds is faith in Allah and jihad in His path."
"956","[AI-translation] 'Ala' bin Ziyad, he said: A man asked Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-'As, saying: Which of the believers is best in Islam? He said: The best of the believers in Islam is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. The best jihad is the one who strives against himself for the sake of Allah. And the best of the emigrants is the one who strives against himself and his desires for the sake of Allah. He said: Did you say this, O Abdullah bin Amr, or the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him? He said: Rather, the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said it."
"957","[AI-translation] From Amr bin Abasa, elevated: The best emigration is that you abandon what your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, dislikes."
"958","[AI-translation] From Fadalah ibn 'Ubayd that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: ""Prosperous is he who is guided to Islam, and whose livelihood is bare sufficiency, and who is content with it."
"959","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: ""I fight the people until they testify that there is no god but Allah and believe in me and in what I have brought. If they do that, they have protected from me their blood and their wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"960","On the authority of Abū Sakhr al-ʿUqaylī: A man from the Bedouins narrated to me, saying: ""I brought merchandise to Medina during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When I had finished my selling, I said to myself: 'I will surely meet this man [the Prophet] so that I may hear from him.' Then I encountered him walking between Abū Bakr and ʿUmar. I followed behind them until they came upon a Jewish man who had spread out the Torah and was reading from it, consoling himself with it over a son of his who had died, [a son who was] like the finest of youths and the most beautiful of them.The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I adjure you by the One Who sent down the Torah: do you find in your Book my description and my coming forth [as a Prophet]?' He gestured with his head like this—meaning: no.His son said: 'Rather, by the One Who sent down the Torah, we surely find in our Book your description and your coming forth, and I bear witness that there is no deity but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah.'The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Remove the Jew from your brother'—meaning the son of the Jew who had accepted Islam. Then he took charge of shrouding him, embalming him, and praying over him."""
"961","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: ""Increase your testimony that there is no god but Allah, before a barrier is set between you and it, and instruct it to your dying."
"962","[AI-translation] Ashja'i who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: ""Lo, they are but four: that you do not associate anything with Allah, that you do not kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, that you do not commit adultery, and that you do not steal."" He said: ""I am no more miserly regarding them than I was when I heard them from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him."
"963","[AI-translation] From Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas that he used to pray the last 'Isha' in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, then pray the Witr as one rak'ah, not adding to it. It was said to him: ""Do you pray Witr as one rak'ah, not adding to it, O Abu Ishaq?"" He would say: ""Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: 'The one who does not sleep until he prays Witr is resolute.'"
"964","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr who said: Al-'As ibn Wa'il vowed during the pre-Islamic period of ignorance to slaughter a hundred camels, and Hisham ibn al-'As slaughtered his share of fifty camels, and 'Amr asked the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, about that. He said: ""As for your father, had he affirmed Tawhid, and you fasted and gave charity on his behalf, that would have benefited him."
"965","[AI-translation] From 'Adi ibn Hatim who said: I came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and on my neck was a gold cross. He said: ""O 'Adi, cast off this idol."" And I heard him reciting in Surah Bara'ah: ""They have taken their rabbis and monks as lords besides Allah"" (At-Tawbah: 31). I said: ""We do not worship them."" He said: ""Indeed, they did not worship them; but when they made something lawful for them, they took it as lawful, and when they forbade something to them, they forbade it? (That was their worship of them)."
"966","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger, and that they face our Qiblah, and eat our slaughtered animals, and that they pray our prayer. When they do that, (then) their blood and their wealth have become forbidden to us except by its right. For them is what is for the Muslims, and upon them is what is upon the Muslims."
"967","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah who said: He, peace be upon him, said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. So whoever says there is no god but Allah has protected from me his wealth and himself except by its right, and his reckoning is upon Allah."
"968","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and establish the prayer and give the Zakah. When they do that, they have protected from me their blood and their wealth except by the right of Islam, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"969","[AI-translation] Jabir reported: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they say 'There is no god but Allah.' So if they say 'There is no god but Allah,' their blood and wealth are protected from me except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."" Then he recited: ""You are only a reminder. You are not over them a controller."" (Al-Ghashiyah)."
"970","[AI-translation] Jabir reported: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) commanded us to do four things and forbade us from five: When you sleep, close your door, tie your waterskin, cover your vessel, and extinguish your lamp, for Satan does not open a door, nor untie a knot, nor uncover a cover, and the mischievous mouse may burn down the house of its inhabitants. Do not eat with your left hand, do not drink with your left hand, do not walk in one sandal, do not wrap yourself in the Samma' garment, and do not wrap yourself in an Izar exposing your nakedness."
"971","[AI-translation] Husayn reported: Husayn came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: ""What do you think of a man who maintained ties of kinship and honored the guest, who died before your time?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""My father and your father are in the Fire."" No twenty nights passed before he died as a polytheist."
"972","[AI-translation] Aishah reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Satan comes to one of you and says, 'Who created you?' He says, 'Allah.' Then he says, 'Who created Allah?' If any of you finds this, let him read: 'I believe in Allah and His messengers,' for that will dispel it from him."
"973","[AI-translation] Hudhayfah reported: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The thing I fear most for you is a man who reads the Quran, until when its radiance is seen upon him and he is a support for Islam, he strips it off and throws it behind his back, and attacks his neighbor with the sword, accusing him of Shirk."" I said: ""O Prophet of Allah! Which of them is more deserving of Shirk, the accuser or the accused?"" He said: ""Rather, the accuser."
"974","[AI-translation] Mahmud bin Labid reported: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The thing I fear most for you is minor Shirk."" They asked: ""And what is minor Shirk?"" He said: ""Riya' (showing off). Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says to its people on the Day of Resurrection when He recompenses people: 'Go to those whom you used to show off to in the world, and see if you find any reward with them.'"
"975","[AI-translation] Ka'b bin Malik reported: When death approached Ka'b, Umm Mubashshir bint Al-Bara' bin Ma'rur entered upon him and said: ""O Abu Abd al-Rahman, if you meet my son, convey my salam to him."" He said: ""May Allah forgive you, O Umm Mubashshir, we are too preoccupied for that."" She said: ""O Abu Abd al-Rahman, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say, 'The souls of the believers are in the crops of green birds that hang on the trees of Paradise'?"" He said: ""Yes."" She said: ""That is it."
"976","[AI-translation] Abdullah bin Mas'ud reported from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) that he said: ""Islam began as something strange, and it will return to being strange as it began, so Tuba is for the strangers."" It was asked: ""Who are they, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""Those who reform when the people become corrupt."
"977","[AI-translation] Mujahid reported: I went out to Iraq, and Abdullah bin Umar bade us farewell. When he parted from us, he said: ""I do not have anything to give you, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: 'Allah preserves whatever is entrusted to Him, and I entrust Allah with your religion, your trust, and the final deeds of your works.'"
"978","[AI-translation] Mu'awiyah bin Hakim (bin Hazam) reported from his father who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Verily, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not accept the repentance of a servant who disbelieves after his Islam."
"979","On the authority of Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah (mighty and sublime be He) said: ""Whosoever shows enmity to a friend of Mine, I shall be at war with him. My servant does not draw near to Me with anything more beloved to Me than the religious duties I have imposed upon him, and My servant continues to draw near to Me with supererogatory works so that I shall love him. When I love him, I am his hearing with which he hears, his seeing with which he sees, his hand with which he strikes, and his foot with which he walks. Were he to ask [something] of Me, I would surely give it to him, and were he to ask Me for refuge, I would surely grant him it. I do not hesitate about anything as much as I hesitate about [seizing] the soul of My faithful servant: he hates death and I hate hurting him."""
"980","[AI-translation] From Yunus bin Maysarah bin Halbas who said: We entered upon Yazid bin Al-Aswad, and Wathilah entered upon him. When he looked at him, he extended his hand, so he took his hand and wiped his face and chest with it, because he had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, with it. He said to him: ""O Yazid, what is your thought regarding your Lord?"" He said: ""Good."" He said: ""Then rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: 'Allah, the Exalted, says: I am as my servant thinks of Me. If he thinks good, then it is good, and if he thinks evil, then it is evil.'"
"981","[AI-translation] Adra' that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, was informed that a man in the mosque was prolonging the prayer. He came to him and took him by the shoulder, then said: ""Allah is pleased with ease for this Ummah and dislikes hardship for them"" - he said this three times - ""and this one has taken to hardship and abandoned ease."
"982","Ibn ʿAbbās said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: ""And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed—those are the disbelievers"" (Al-Māʾidah: 44); ""those are the wrongdoers"" (Al-Māʾidah: 45); ""those are the defiantly disobedient"" (Al-Māʾidah: 47).Ibn ʿAbbās said: Allah revealed these verses concerning two factions of the Jews. One of them had subjugated the other during the pre-Islamic period of ignorance (Jāhiliyyah) until they agreed and made a settlement that every person killed by the dominant faction (al-ʿAzīzah) from the subjugated faction (al-Dhallīlah), their blood money would be fifty wasqs; and every person killed by the subjugated faction from the dominant faction, their blood money would be one hundred wasqs. They remained upon this until the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Medina. Both factions were humbled by the arrival of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and at that time he had not yet manifested [authority] nor had they submitted to him, while he was [still] under the treaty.Then the subjugated faction killed a man from the dominant faction. The dominant faction sent to the subjugated faction demanding they send them one hundred wasqs. The subjugated faction said: ""Was this ever the case in the lifetime of either of them, that their religion is one, their lineage is one, their land is one, yet the blood money of some of them is half the blood money of others? We only gave you this as oppression from you against us and fear of you. But now that Muḥammad has come, we will not give you that.""War nearly broke out between them. Then they agreed to make the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the arbitrator between them. Then the dominant faction mentioned [the matter] and said: ""By Allah, Muḥammad will not give you double what he gives them from you. And they spoke the truth: we only gave this as oppression from us and subjugation of them.""So they secretly sent people to Muḥammad to inform them of his opinion: ""If he gives you what you want, you will accept his judgment; and if he does not give you [what you want], beware, and do not accept his judgment."" So they secretly sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some people from the hypocrites to inform them of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ opinion.When they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Allah informed His Messenger of their entire affair and what they intended. Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: ""O Messenger, let not those grieve you who hasten into disbelief..."" (Al-Māʾidah: 41) and ""And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed—those are the defiantly disobedient"" (Al-Māʾidah).Then he said concerning the two of them: ""By Allah, they were revealed, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, meant them both."""
"983","[AI-translation] From Abdullah, raised to the Prophet: ""Allah, Almighty and Majestic, surely supports this religion by a wicked man."
"984","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: ""Allah, Almighty and Majestic, laughs at two men, one of whom kills the other, then Allah enters them both into Paradise. One of them is a disbeliever, so he kills the other, then he embraces Islam, fights in the way of Allah, and is killed."
"985","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""Allah will send for this Ummah at the head of every hundred years someone who will renew its religion for it."
"986","[AI-translation] From Hudhayfah, raised to the Prophet: ""Allah is the Creator of every maker and his making."
"987","[AI-translation] Dahhak bin Qais who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Allah says: I am the best partner. Whoever associates anyone with Me, then he is for My partner. O people, make your deeds purely for Allah, for Allah, Almighty and Majestic, does not accept from the deed except what is pure for Him. And do not say: 'This is for Allah and for kinship,' while none of it is for Allah! And do not say: 'This is for Allah and for your faces,' for indeed it is for your faces, and none of it is for Allah."
"988","[AI-translation] As who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Faith wears out within one of you just as a garment wears out, so ask Allah to renew the faith in your hearts."
"989","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""The first thing Allah created was the Pen. He took it with His right hand, and both His hands are right."" He said: ""He wrote the world and what is in it of deeds done, whether piety or wickedness, fresh or dry, and recorded it in the Remembrance. Then he said: 'Read if you wish: {This, Our record, speaks about you with the truth. Indeed, We were to transcribe whatever you used to do} (Al-Jathiyah).' For is a copy made except from an affair that has already been completed?"
"990","On the authority of Sulayman ibn Yasar, who said: The people dispersed from around Abu Hurayrah, whereupon a man from the people of Syria, called Natil, said to him: ""O Shaykh, narrate to us a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."" He said: ""Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: 'The first of people to be judged on the Day of Resurrection will be a man who was martyred. He will be brought forth, and Allah will make him recognize His blessings, and he will recognize them. Allah will say: ""What did you do with them?"" He will say: ""I fought in Your cause until I was martyred."" Allah will say: ""You have lied. Rather, you fought so that it would be said: 'He is brave.' And so it was said."" Then it will be ordered that he be dragged on his face until he is thrown into the Fire.And a man who acquired knowledge, taught it, and recited the Quran. He will be brought forth, and Allah will make him recognize His blessings, and he will recognize them. Allah will say: ""What did you do with them?"" He will say: ""I acquired knowledge, taught it, and recited the Quran for Your sake."" Allah will say: ""You have lied. Rather, you acquired knowledge so that it would be said: 'He is a scholar,' and you recited the Quran so that it would be said: 'He is a reciter.' And so it was said."" Then it will be ordered that he be dragged on his face until he is thrown into the Fire.And a man whom Allah made wealthy and gave him from all kinds of wealth. He will be brought forth, and Allah will make him recognize His blessings, and he will recognize them. Allah will say: ""What did you do with them?"" He will say: ""I did not leave any path in which You love that money be spent except that I spent in it for Your sake."" Allah will say: ""You have lied. Rather, you did it so that it would be said: 'He is generous.' And so it was said."" Then it will be ordered that he be dragged on his face and then thrown into the Fire.'"""
"991","[AI-translation] Rahman who both said: We met Abdullah bin Umar and mentioned to him the divine decree and what they say concerning it. He mentioned something similar, and added: A man from Muzaynah or Juhaynah asked: ""O Messenger of Allah, in what are we acting? Is it in something that has already passed and gone, or in something that is newly begun now?"" He said: ""In something that has already passed and gone."" The man, or some of the people, said: ""Then what is the deed for?"" He said: ""The people of Paradise are facilitated for the deeds of the people of Paradise, and the people of the Fire are facilitated for the deeds of the people of the Fire."
"992","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, he said: A funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and they praised it well, so he said: ""It is decreed."" Then another passed by and they praised it evilly, so he said: ""It is decreed."" Then he said: ""You are witnesses against one another."
"993","On the authority of Al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: He heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioning the Raqim (the Inscription/the Companions of the Cave), and he said: ""Indeed, three men were in a cave. A rock fell from the mountain and blocked the entrance of the cave, sealing them in. One of them said: 'Let each of you recall a good deed you have done, perhaps Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will have mercy on us through His mercy because of it.' A man among them said: 'I once did a good deed. I had laborers working for me. My workers came to me, and I hired each man for a known wage. One day, a man came to me in the middle of the day, and I hired him for half the wage of his companions. He worked for the remainder of his day just as each of his companions had worked for their entire day. I felt it incumbent upon me (in conscience) not to give him less than what I had hired his companions for, because he had exerted himself in his work. One of them said: ""Do you give this man the same as you gave us, when he only worked half a day?"" I said: ""O servant of Allah, I have not wronged you anything of your agreement; rather, this is my wealth, I dispose of it as I wish."" He became angry, left, and forfeited his wage. I set aside his due in a corner of the house, as Allah willed. Then, after that, some cattle passed by me, so I bought a heifer with it. It grew as Allah willed. After a while, an old, weak man passed by me whom I did not recognize. He said: ""I have a right due upon you."" He reminded me of it until I recognized him. I said: ""It is you I seek; this is your right."" I presented all of it (the cattle) to him. He said: ""O servant of Allah, do not mock me; if you are not giving it to me in charity, then give me my right."" I said: ""By Allah, I do not mock you; it is indeed your right, I have no share in it."" I handed it all over to him. ""O Allah, if I did that seeking Your Face, then relieve us from our distress."" The rock split open until they could see out of it and they saw (the sky). The second one said: 'I once did a good deed. I had surplus wealth. People were afflicted with hardship (famine). A woman came to me asking for a favor (help). I said: ""By Allah, I have nothing to give you but myself (i.e., I cannot help you except by taking you as a wife/concubine)."" She refused. She went away, then returned and adjured me by Allah. I refused her and said: ""By Allah, I have nothing but myself."" She refused and left. She mentioned it to her husband, who said to her: ""Give him yourself, and I will provide for your family."" She returned to me and adjured me by Allah. I refused her and said: ""By Allah, I have nothing but myself."" When she saw that, she submitted herself to me. When I uncovered her and intended to have intercourse with her, she trembled beneath me. I said to her: ""What is the matter with you?"" She said: ""I fear Allah, Lord of the Worlds."" I said to her: ""You feared Him in hardship, but I did not fear Him in ease."" I left her and gave her what was due to me for having uncovered her. ""O Allah, if I did that seeking Your Face, then relieve us from our distress."" The rock split further until they recognized (the way out) and it became clear to them. The third one said: 'I once did a good deed. I had two elderly parents, and I had sheep. I used to feed my parents and give them drink, then return to my sheep. One day, rain fell which detained me, so I did not leave until evening. I came to my family, took my milking vessel, and milked my sheep while standing. I went to my parents and found them asleep. It was hard for me to wake them, and it was hard for me to leave my sheep (without milking them for them). I did not cease sitting with my milking vessel in my hand until dawn woke them. Then I gave them drink. ""O Allah, if I did that seeking Your Face, then relieve us from our distress."" Al-Nu'man said: ""It is as if I hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The rock split wide open (Tāq), and Allah relieved them, so they came out."""
"994","[AI-translation] From Anas that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""The Dajjal will fold up the whole earth except for Makkah and Madinah."" He said: ""So he will come to Madinah and find at every pass of its passes rows of angels. He will come to the salt flats of Al-Jurf and pitch his tent, then Madinah will shake with three tremors, and every male and female hypocrite will go out to him."
"995","[AI-translation] Zuraqi, he said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, about 'azl, and said: ""My wife is nursing and I dislike that she becomes pregnant."" So the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Whatever has been decreed in the womb will be."
"996","[AI-translation] Asadi, he said: Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, entered upon a woman and saw upon her a talisman of red [thread], so he cut it violently, then said: ""The family of Abd Allah are free from shirk."" And he said: ""Among what we have memorized from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, is that charms (ruqa), amulets (tamaim), and love spells (tiwalah) are from shirk."
"997","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, he said: Three things I heard regarding Banu Tamim from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family; I will never hate Banu Tamim after them ever. 'Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, had a vow to free a slave from the offspring of Isma'il. Then a group of captives from Banu Al-'Anbar was taken. When those captives were brought, the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said to her: ""If it pleases you to fulfill your vow, free a slave from these."" And he said: ""He made them from the offspring of Isma'il."" And some camels from the camels of charity were brought, and when he saw them, their excellence amazed him. He said: He said, ""These are the camels of my people,"" so he made them his people. He said: And he said, ""They are the fiercest in fighting in the great battles."
"998","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, he said: ""Satan has despaired of being worshipped in this land of yours, but he is satisfied with what you belittle."
"999","[AI-translation] Ansari, elevated [to the Prophet]: ""Verily, Satan has despaired of being worshipped by those who pray in the Arabian Peninsula, but [he is content] with sowing discord among them."
"1000","Sabrah ibn Abi Fakih reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saying: ""Indeed, Satan sat in wait for the son of Adam on his paths. He sat for him on the path of Islam and said: 'Will you embrace Islam and abandon your religion and the religion of your fathers and grandfathers?' He disobeyed him and became Muslim. Then he sat for him on the path of Hijrah (migration) and said: 'Will you migrate and leave your land and your sky?' The example of the migrant is only like that of a horse tethered by its rope. He disobeyed him and migrated. Then he sat for him on the path of Jihad and said: 'Will you fight? It is a struggle of self and wealth; you fight and get killed, then your wife remarries and your wealth is divided.' He disobeyed him and fought. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'Whoever does that, it is a right upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to admit him into Paradise. Whoever is killed, it is a right upon Allah to admit him into Paradise. If he drowns, it is a right upon Allah to admit him into Paradise. Or if his mount throws him and breaks his neck, it is a right upon Allah to admit him into Paradise.'"""
"1001","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, he said: They mentioned bad omens in the presence of the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and he said: ""If there is bad luck in anything, it is in the house, the woman, and the horse."
"1002","On the authority of Ṭufayl ibn Sakhbara, the maternal brother of ʿĀʾishah, who said: He saw in a dream as if he passed by a group of Jews. He said: ""Who are you?"" They said: ""We are the Jews."" He said: ""You are the people, were it not that you claim that ʿUzayr is the son of Allah."" The Jews said: ""And you are the people, were it not that you say: 'What Allah wills and what Muḥammad wills!'"" Then he passed by a group of Christians. He said: ""Who are you?"" They said: ""We are the Christians."" He said: ""You are the people, were it not that you say the Messiah is the son of Allah."" They said: ""And you are the people, were it not that you say: 'What Allah wills and what Muḥammad wills!'"" When morning came, he informed whoever informed [others] of it, then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said: ""Did you inform anyone of it?"" He said: ""Yes."" When they prayed, he addressed them, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: ""Ṭufayl saw a vision and informed whoever informed of you about it. And you used to say a word which modesty from you prevented me from forbidding you from it."" He said: ""Do not say: 'What Allah wills and what Muḥammad wills.'"""
"1003","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, elevated [to the Prophet]: ""Verily, the evil eye can overwhelm a man, by the permission of Allah, until he ascends a high peak and then falls from it."
"1004","[AI-translation] Hajjaj: ""Did not the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, narrate to us that in Thaqif there is a liar and a destroyer? As for the liar, we have seen him, and as for the destroyer, I consider no one but you to be him."" ( )"
"1005","[AI-translation] 'As (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) say: ""Indeed, the hearts of all the children of Adam are between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful like one heart; He turns it however He wills."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, Turner of hearts, turn our hearts towards Your obedience."
"1006","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A people will come after me; one of them would wish to ransom his family and wealth for a sight of me."
"1007","[AI-translation] Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Islam has signs and landmarks like the landmarks of a road. Among them are: that you believe in Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establishing the prayer, giving the zakah, fasting Ramadan, performing Hajj to the House, enjoining good and forbidding evil, and giving salam to your family when you enter upon them, and giving salam to the people when you pass by them. Whoever leaves any of that has left a portion of Islam, and whoever leaves all of them has turned his back to Islam."
"1008","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Furat ibn Hayyan that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) ordered his execution. He was a spy for Abu Sufyan and was an ally of a man from the Ansar. He passed by a gathering of the Ansar and said: ""I am a Muslim."" A man from the Ansar said: ""O Messenger of Allah, he says: I am a Muslim."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There are men among you whom we entrust to their faith, among them is Furat ibn Hayyan."
"1009","Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with him) reported: He went on an expedition with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) toward Najd. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) returned, he returned with him. The midday rest overtook them in a valley full of thorny trees. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) dismounted, and the people dispersed among the thorny trees, seeking shade under the trees. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) dismounted under a samurah tree and hung his sword on it. Jābir said: We slept a brief sleep, when suddenly the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was calling us. We came to him, and there was a Bedouin sitting with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This man unsheathed my sword while I was sleeping. I woke up and it was in his hand, drawn. He said to me: 'Who will protect you from me?' I said: 'Allah.' So here he is, sitting."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not punish him."
"1010","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Indeed, this religion is ease, and no one will overburden himself in the religion except that it overcomes him. So be steadfast, aim near perfection, give glad tidings, and seek help in the morning, the evening, and a portion of the late night."
"1011","Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Khayr said: While we were at al-Mirbad, a Bedouin with disheveled hair came upon us, carrying a piece of leather or a piece of a sack. We said: ""It seems this man is not from the people of this town."" He said: ""Yes, this is a document written for me by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."" The people said: ""Bring it forth."" So I took it and read it, and it contained: ""In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is a document from Muhammad the Prophet, Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to Banu Zuhayr ibn Uqaysh."" Abu al-Ala said: ""They are a clan of Ukl. 'If you bear witness that there is no deity but Allah, establish the prayer, give the zakah, separate from the polytheists, give from the spoils the fifth (khums) and the Prophet's share ﷺ—and perhaps he said: and his chosen portion (safiyyah)—then you are secure under the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger.'"""
"1012","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""There is nothing that brings you closer to Paradise except that I have commanded you to do it, and there is nothing that brings you closer to the Fire except that I have forbidden you from it. The Ruh al-Qudus breathed into my heart: No soul will die until it completes its provision. So fear Allah and be moderate in seeking provision, and let not the delay of provision drive you to seek it through disobedience to Allah, for what is with Allah is only attained through obedience to Him."
"1013","From ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn, that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās said: A man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, from the Anṣār, informed me: While they were sitting one night with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a star was shot forth and it lit up. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: ""What did you used to say in the Days of Ignorance when a star like this was shot?"" They said: ""Allah and His Messenger know best. We used to say: 'A great man has been born this night, and a great man has died.'"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""It is not shot for the death of anyone nor for his life. Rather, when our Lord, Blessed and Exalted is His Name, decrees a matter, the bearers of the Throne glorify Him; then the inhabitants of the heaven nearest to them glorify, until the glorification reaches the inhabitants of this lowest heaven. Then those who are near the bearers of the Throne ask the bearers of the Throne: 'What did your Lord say?' So they inform them of what He said. Then the inhabitants of the heavens seek information from one another until the news reaches this lowest heaven. The jinn snatch the hearing, then they cast it to their allies, and they are pelted with it. Whatever they bring as it truly is, is true; but they distort it and add to it."""
"1014","On the authority of Salama ibn Nufayl al-Sakuni, who said: I drew near to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) until my knees almost touched his thigh. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Horses have been abandoned, weapons have been laid down, and some people claim there is no more fighting! He said: They lied! Now fighting has come. There will never cease to be a group from my Ummah standing upon the truth, prevailing over people. Allah will cause the hearts of people who fight them to deviate, so that they may harm them. And he said, while turning his back toward Yemen: I perceive the breath of the Most Merciful from here — gesturing toward Yemen. And it has been revealed to me that I am restrained, not remaining long, and you will follow me in groups. And goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Judgment, and their owners are rewarded for them."
"1015","Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out to us one day and said: ""I saw in a dream as if Gabriel was at my head and Michael at my feet. One of them said to the other: 'Strike a parable for him.' He said: 'Listen, may your ear hear, and understand, may your heart comprehend. Verily, your parable and the parable of your nation is like that of a king who took a dwelling, then built a house in it, then placed a table in it, then sent a messenger inviting people to his food. Some of them answered the messenger, and some left him. So Allah is the King, the dwelling is Islam, the house is Paradise, and you, O Muhammad, are the messenger. Whoever answers you enters Islam, and whoever enters Islam enters Paradise, and whoever enters Paradise eats what is in it.'"""
"1016","From Abu Umamah, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his military expeditions. He said: A man passed by a cave containing some water. He considered staying in that cave, sustaining himself with the water in it, eating the herbs around it, and renouncing the world! Then he said: ""If only I went to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and mentioned this to him; if he permits me, I will do it, otherwise I will not."" So he came to him and said: ""O Prophet of Allah! I passed by a cave with enough water and herbs to sustain me, and I considered staying in it and renouncing the world."" The Prophet ﷺ said: ""I was not sent with Judaism nor Christianity, but I was sent with the easy Hanifiyyah (pure monotheism). And by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, a morning or evening expedition in the cause of Allah is better than the world and everything in it. And the standing of one of you in the battle line is better than his prayer for sixty years."""
"1017","[AI-translation] Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me on the morning of al-'Aqabah while he was standing on his mount: ""Pick up for me."" So I picked up for him some pebbles the size of khadhf pebbles, and I placed them in his hand. He said: ""With ones like these,"" twice. And he said with his hand—Yahya, one of its narrators, gestured that he raised it—and said: ""Beware of exaggeration in religion, for those before you were destroyed by exaggeration in religion."
"1018","[AI-translation] Khuza'i said: A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah, is there an end for Islam?"" He said: ""Any household of the Arabs or non-Arabs that Allah intends good for, He brings Islam upon them."" He said: ""Then what?"" He said: ""Then trials will occur like shadows."" A man said: ""Never, by Allah, if Allah wills."" He said: ""Yes, by the One in Whose hand is my soul, you will then return in them like black snakes poured forth, striking the necks of one another."
"1019","On the authority of Abū ʿĀmir al-Ashʿarī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A man from among them was killed at Awtās. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""O Abū ʿĀmir, why did you not change it?"" He recited this verse: ""O you who have believed, upon you is [responsibility for] yourselves. Those who have gone astray will not harm you when you have been guided"" (Al-Māʾidah: 105). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) became angry and said: ""Where have you gone? Rather, it is: 'O you who have believed, those who have gone astray from among the disbelievers will not harm you when you have been guided.'""And al-Ṭabarānī narrated it with the wording: On the authority of Abū ʿĀmir, that there was something among them, so he was delayed from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What held you back?"" He said: ""I recited this verse: 'O you who have believed, upon you is [responsibility for] yourselves. Those who have gone astray will not harm you when you have been guided.'"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: ""Those who have gone astray from among the disbelievers will not harm you when you have been guided."""
"1020","[AI-translation] Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whenever any man says to his brother, 'O disbeliever,' it surely falls upon one of them. If he is as he said, then so be it; otherwise, it returns upon him. And in a narration: Upon the other."
"1021","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Faith is seventy-something branches. The lowest of them is removing harm from the road, and the highest of them is the saying: 'There is no god but Allah.'"
"1022","[AI-translation] From 'Amr ibn 'Abasah, marfu': Faith is patience and tolerance."
"1023","[AI-translation] From Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, say: Faith is Yemeni, like this, up to Lakhm and Judham."
"1024","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, who said: Faith is Yemeni, and disbelief is from the direction of the East. Tranquility is among the people of the sheep, and showing off and pride are among the people of the noisy cattle, the people of the woolen tents, and the people of the horses. The Masih will come from the direction of the East, and his destination is Madinah, until when he reaches the back of Uhud, the angels will meet him and turn his face towards Sham. There he will perish, there he will perish."
"1025","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, say: I spent the night reciting to the jinn as companions at al-Hajun."
"1026","On the authority of Abu Sufyan ibn Harb: Heraclius sent for him in a caravan of Quraysh. They were merchants in Syria during the truce that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had made with Abu Sufyan and the disbelievers of Quraysh. They came to him while they were in Jerusalem. He summoned them to his court, and around him were the great men of Rome. Then he called them and called for his translator. He said: ""Which of you is closest in lineage to this man who claims to be a Prophet?"" Abu Sufyan said: I said: ""I am the closest of them in lineage to him."" He said: ""Bring him close to me and bring his companions near, and make them stand behind his back."" Then he said to his translator: ""Tell them: I am going to question this man. If he lies to me, then contradict him. By Allah, were it not for the shame of them attributing a lie to me, I would have lied about him.""Then the first thing he asked me about him was: ""How is his lineage among you?"" I said: ""He is of noble lineage among us."" He said: ""Has anyone among you ever said this claim before him?"" I said: ""No."" He said: ""Was there a king among his forefathers?"" I said: ""No."" He said: ""Do the nobles of the people follow him, or the weak?"" I said: ""Rather, the weak."" He said: ""Are they increasing or decreasing?"" I said: ""Rather, they are increasing."" He said: ""Does anyone apostatize from his religion out of displeasure after entering it?"" I said: ""No."" He said: ""Did you use to accuse him of lying before he said what he said?"" I said: ""No."" He said: ""Does he betray?"" I said: ""No. And we are in a truce with him, but we do not know what he will do during it."" He said: ""I could not find a word to insert anything other than this word."" He said: ""Have you fought him?"" I said: ""Yes."" He said: ""How was your fighting with him?"" I said: ""The war between us and him is alternating; he inflicts casualties on us and we inflict casualties on him."" He said: ""What does he command you?"" I said: ""He says: Worship Allah alone and do not associate anything with Him, and abandon what your fathers say. And he commands us to pray, speak the truth, be chaste, and maintain family ties.""He said to the translator: ""Say to him: I asked you about his lineage, and you mentioned that he is of noble lineage among you. Thus are the Messengers sent among the lineage of their people. I asked you: Has anyone among you said this claim? You mentioned: No. I said: If someone had said this claim before him, I would have said: A man imitating a saying said before him. I asked you: Was there a king among his forefathers? You mentioned: No. I said: If there had been a king among his forefathers, I would have said: A man seeking his father's kingdom. I asked you: Did you use to accuse him of lying before he said what he said? You mentioned: No. So I know that he would not leave off lying to people and then lie to Allah. I asked you: Did the nobles follow him or the weak? You mentioned: The weak followed him. And they are the followers of the Messengers. I asked you: Are they increasing or decreasing? You mentioned: They are increasing. And thus is the affair of faith until it is complete. I asked you: Does anyone apostatize out of displeasure for his religion after entering it? You mentioned: No. And thus is faith when its delight enters the hearts. I asked you: Does he betray? You mentioned: No. And thus the Messengers do not betray. I asked you: What does he command you? You mentioned: He commands you to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, and forbids you from worshipping idols, and commands you to pray, speak the truth, be chaste, and maintain family ties. If what you say is true, he will possess the place of these two feet of mine. And I knew that he would appear, but I did not think he would be from you. If I knew I would reach him, I would exert myself to meet him, and if I were with him, I would wash his feet.""Then he called for the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) which Dihyah had brought to the Great Man of Busra, who handed it to Heraclius. He read it, and it said: ""In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad, the servant of Allah and His Messenger, to Heraclius, the Great Man of Rome. Peace be upon him who follows the guidance. To proceed: I invite you with the invitation of Islam. Accept Islam and you will be safe; Allah will give you your reward twice. But if you turn away, then upon you is the sin of the Ariyyeen."" [Aal Imran: 64].Abu Sufyan said: When he said what he said and finished reading the letter, there was a great clamor around him, and the voices rose, and we were expelled. I said to my companions when we were expelled: ""The affair of the son of Abu Kabshah has become prominent; indeed, the King of the Banu al-Asfar fears him."" I continued to be certain that he would prevail until Allah entered Islam into my heart.Ibn al-Natur was the owner of Jerusalem and Heraclius's superior over the Christians of Syria. He narrates that when Heraclius came to Jerusalem, he woke up one day in a bad mood. Some of his patriarchs said: ""We have found your condition strange."" Ibn al-Natur said: Heraclius was a diviner who looked at the stars. He said to them when they asked him: ""I saw last night, when I looked at the stars, that the King of the Circumcised has appeared. Who among this nation circumcises?"" They said: ""None circumcise except the Jews. So do not let their matter concern you, and write to the cities of your kingdom to kill the Jews among them."" While they were on this matter, a man was brought to Heraclius, sent by the King of Ghassan, informing him about the news of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). When Heraclius questioned him, he said: ""Go and see: is he circumcised or not?"" They looked at him and reported that he was circumcised. He asked him about the Arabs, and he said: ""They circumcise."" Heraclius said: ""This is the kingdom of this nation that has appeared.""Then Heraclius wrote to a friend of his in Rome who was his peer in knowledge. And Heraclius set out for Homs. He did not stay long in Homs until a letter came to him from his friend agreeing with Heraclius's opinion on the emergence of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and that he is a Prophet. Heraclius permitted the great men of Rome into a palace of his in Homs. Then he ordered its doors to be locked. Then he appeared and said: ""O Romans, do you desire success, guidance, and that your kingdom remain firm? Then pledge allegiance to this Prophet."" They rushed like wild donkeys toward the doors, but found them locked. When Heraclius saw their aversion and despaired of their faith, he said: ""Return them to me."" And he said: ""I said my previous statement only to test the firmness of your religion."" So they prostrated to him and were pleased with him. That was the end of Heraclius's affair."
"1027","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, marfu': Ponder upon the blessings of Allah, and do not ponder upon Allah."
"1028","[AI-translation] From Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three things will not cease to be in my Ummah: boasting about lineages, wailing, and al-anwa'."
"1029","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, marfu': Three practices of the people of Jahiliyyah that the people of Islam will not abandon: wailing, seeking rain through al-anwa', and... Thus I said to Sa'id (meaning al-Maqburi): And what is it? He said: The claim of Jahiliyyah: 'O family of so-and-so! O family of so-and-so! O family of so-and-so!'"
"1030","[AI-translation] Ghadari, marfu': Three, whoever does them has tasted the taste of faith: one who worships Allah alone and that there is no god but Allah, and gives the zakat of his wealth, with a pleased soul, recurring upon him every year, and does not give the old, the worn-out, the sick, nor the vile choice, but from the middle of your wealth, for Allah has not asked you for its best, nor has He commanded you to give its worst."
"1031","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Three traits, whoever possesses them will find the sweetness and taste of faith: that Allah, the Almighty and Majestic, and His Messenger are more beloved to him than anything besides them, that he loves for the sake of Allah and hates for the sake of Allah, and that a great fire be kindled and he fall into it is more beloved to him than to associate anything with Allah."
"1032","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him: Three from whom Allah will not accept any voluntary act nor any obligatory act: the undutiful son, the one who reminds others of his favors, and the denier of divine predestination."
"1033","[AI-translation] Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, raised [to the Prophet]: Three persons will be given their reward twice: a man who had a female slave, so he disciplined her and did well in his disciplining of her, and taught her and did well in his teaching of her, then he freed her and married her; a slave who fulfilled the right of his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and the right of his masters; and a man who believed in his Book and in Muhammad, peace be upon him."
"1034","[AI-translation] On the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and asked about al-'azl. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: If you were to pour the water from which the child is formed onto a rock, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, would bring forth from it, or a child would emerge from it. And Allah will surely create a soul that He is to create."
"1035","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said: ""The Angel of Death came to me—and in another version: 'The Angel of Death comes to people visibly'—until he came to Moses (peace be upon him) and said: 'Answer your Lord.' So Moses (peace be upon him) struck the eye of the Angel of Death and gouged it out. The angel returned to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and said: 'O Lord! You sent me to a servant of Yours who does not want death, and he has gouged out my eye (and were it not for his honor upon You, I would have caused him distress).' So Allah restored his eye to him and said: 'Return to My servant and say to him: Do you want life? If you want life, then place your hand on the back of an ox, and whatever hairs your hand covers, you will live for a year for each hair.' He said: 'O Lord! Then what?' He said: 'Then death.' He said: 'Then let it be now.' He said: 'O Lord, cause me to die near the Sacred Land, a stone's throw away.' (He said: 'So he smelled it a sniff and his soul was taken.' He said: 'Then after that he came to people secretly.') The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said: 'By Allah, if I were there, I would show you his grave beside the road, at—and in the version: beneath the red sand dune.'"""
"1036","[AI-translation] On the authority of Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Paradise is closer to one of you than the strap of his sandal, and the Fire is likewise."
"1037","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Truthful and Verified one narrated to us, in what he relates from his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, that He said: A good deed is for ten times its like, or I increase it, and a bad deed is for one, or I forgive it. And if you were to meet Me with an earth-full of sins, as long as you do not associate anything with Me, I would meet you with an earth-full of forgiveness."
"1038","[AI-translation] On the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The lawful is clear, and the unlawful is clear, and between the two are doubtful matters. Whoever engages in them is liable to commit a sin, and whoever avoids them is more protective of his religion. It is like a pasturer grazing near a sanctuary, who is bound to fall into it. Every king has a sanctuary, and the sanctuary of Allah is the unlawful."
"1039","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, raised [to the Prophet]: Modesty is from faith, and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, revived my Ummah."
"1040","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abdullah, raised [to the Prophet]: Allah created Yahya bin Zakariya in his mother's womb as a believer, and created Pharaoh in his mother's womb as a disbeliever."
"1041","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abdullah, who said: I heard my father Buraidah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, saying: Five, none knows them except Allah: ""Indeed, with Allah is the knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs. And no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die. Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing, All-Aware."" (Luqman 34)."
"1042","Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I went out one night and found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) walking alone, with no one with him. I thought that he disliked having anyone walk with him. So I began walking in the shadow of the moon. He turned around, saw me, and said: ""Who is this?"" I said: ""Abu Dharr, may Allah make me a ransom for you."" He said: ""O Abu Dharr, come here."" So I walked with him for a while, and he said: ""The most abundant (in wealth) are the least (in reward) on the Day of Resurrection, except for one whom Allah gives wealth and he spends it to his right, left, in front of him, and behind him, and does good with it."" Then I walked with him for a while, and he said to me: ""Sit here."" He made me sit in a depression surrounded by stones. He said to me: ""Sit here until I return to you."" He went off into the rocky ground (al-harrah) until I could no longer see him. He stayed away from me for a long time. Then I heard him as he was returning, saying: ""Even if he stole and even if he committed adultery!"" When he came, I could not restrain myself until I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, may Allah make me a ransom for you, who were you speaking to in the rocky ground? I did not hear anyone reply to you."" He said: ""That was Gabriel (peace be upon him). He met me in the rocky ground and said: 'Give glad tidings to your nation that whoever dies without associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise.' I said: 'O Gabriel, even if he stole and even if he committed adultery?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Even if he stole and even if he committed adultery?' He said: 'Yes, and even if he drank wine.'"""
"1043","Mu'adh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts Ramadan, performs the prayers, and performs Hajj to the House — I do not know whether he mentioned zakat or not — it becomes a right upon Allah to forgive him, whether he emigrates in the cause of Allah or remains in the land where he was born.""Mu'adh said: ""O Messenger of Allah, shall I not inform the people of this?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave the people to work, for in Paradise there are one hundred degrees; the distance between each two degrees is like the distance between the heaven and the earth. And Al-Firdaws is the highest part of Paradise and its middle, and above it is the Throne of the Most Merciful, and from it spring forth the rivers of Paradise. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for Al-Firdaws."""
"1044","[AI-translation] On the authority of Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! We were in a house where our numbers were many and our wealth was abundant, so we moved to another house where our numbers became few and our wealth became little."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Leave it despised."
"1045","[AI-translation] On the authority of Ibn Umar from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: The true dream is one part out of twenty-five parts of prophethood."
"1046","On the authority of Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""I saw my Lord in the most beautiful form. He said: 'In what does the Highest Assembly (of angels) dispute?' I said: 'I do not know.' So He placed His Hand between my shoulders until I felt the coolness of His fingertips between my breast. Then He said: 'In what does the Highest Assembly dispute?' I said: 'Regarding the expiations (kaffārāt) and the degrees (darajāt).' He said: 'And what are the expiations?' I said: 'Perfecting the ablution (wuḍūʾ) during difficulties, walking on foot to the congregational prayers, and waiting for the prayer after the prayer.' He said: 'Then what are the degrees?' I said: 'Feeding food, spreading the greeting of peace (salām), and praying at night while people are asleep.' He said: 'Speak.' I said: 'What shall I say?' He said: 'Say: O Allah! I ask You for the performance of good deeds, the abandonment of evil deeds, and if You intend a trial (fitnah) for a people while I am among them, then take me to You without being afflicted (by that trial).'"""
"1047","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""A man is upon the religion of his close friend, so let one of you look to whom he takes as a close friend."
"1048","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Anas, traced back to the Prophet: ""I asked my Lord for the heedless ones, and He gave them to me. I said: And who are the heedless ones? He said: The offspring of humanity."
"1049","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""Two traits of pre-Islamic ignorance that the people will never abandon: wailing and casting aspersions on lineage."
"1050","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Ibn Abbas: A man said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What are the major sins?"" He said: ""Associating partners with Allah, despairing of the relief of Allah, and despairing of the mercy of Allah."
"1051","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the news of the death of An-Najashi came, the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Pray over him."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Should we pray over an Abyssinian servant (who is not a Muslim)?"" So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: ""And indeed, among the People of the Book are those who believe in Allah and what was revealed to you and what was revealed to them, humbling themselves to Allah. They do not exchange the verses of Allah for a small price. (Aal 'Imran 199)."
"1052","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Razin who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Our Lord laughs at the despair of His servants and the nearness of its opposite."" Abu Razin said: ""Does the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, laugh?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""We will never be devoid of good from a Lord who laughs."
"1053","From Abu Abdur-Rahman Al-Juhani, who said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), two riders appeared. When he saw them, he said: ""Two Kindis from Madh'hij."" When they reached him, they were men from Madh'hij. One of them approached to pledge allegiance to him. When he took his hand, he said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What about someone who saw you, believed in you, believed you, and followed you?"" He said: ""Glad tidings for him."" So he wiped his hand and turned away. Then the other came forward until he took his hand to pledge allegiance. He said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What about someone who believed in you, believed you, and followed you but did not see you?"" He said: ""Glad tidings for him, then glad tidings for him, then glad tidings for him."" So he wiped his hand and turned away."
"1054","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Burdah who said: I came to Aishah and said: ""O Mother! Tell me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family."" She said: ""The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: Birds fly by divine decree, and he used to like good omens."
"1055","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, traced back to the Prophet: ""Superstitious belief in bad omens is polytheism, and none of us is except... but Allah removes it through reliance upon Him."
"1056","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Anas, traced back to the Prophet: ""Injustice is of three types: an injustice that is not left unpunished, an injustice that is forgiven, and an injustice that is not forgiven. As for the injustice that is not forgiven, it is polytheism, which Allah does not forgive. As for the injustice that is forgiven, it is the injustice of a servant between him and his Lord. As for the injustice that is not left unpunished, it is the injustice of the servants against one another, so Allah will exact retribution from some of them against others."
"1057","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: ""I am as my servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he calls upon Me."
"1058","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: ""The son of Adam offends Me when he says, 'O wretched time!' And in a narration: 'He curses time.' So let none of you say, 'O wretched time!' For I am Time; I turn the night and the day, and when I will, I shall take them both."
"1059","[AI-translation] Bara' bin 'Azib from the Prophet (peace be upon him), regarding His saying: ""And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed - then it is those who are the disbelievers."" (44) ""And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed - then it is those who are the wrongdoers."" (45) ""And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed - then it is those who are the defiantly disobedient."" (47), he said: ""All of them are concerning the disbelievers."
"1060","[AI-translation] On the authority of Qutaylah bint Sayfi, a woman from Juhaynah, who said: A rabbi came to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) and said: ""You commit shirk! You say, 'What Allah willed and you willed,' and you say, 'By the Ka'bah.'"" So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Say: 'What Allah willed, then you willed,' and say: 'By the Lord of the Ka'bah.'"
"1061","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abu Hassan, who said: Two men from Banu 'Amir entered upon 'A'ishah and informed her that Abu Hurayrah narrates from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) that he said: ""The people of the pre-Islamic period used to say: 'Evil omens are in the house, the woman, and the horse.'"" She became angry, and a piece of her flew into the sky and a piece into the earth, and she said: ""By the One who sent down the Furqan upon Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) never said that at all. He only said: 'The people of the pre-Islamic period used to see evil omens in that.'"
"1062","[AI-translation] 'Awqi, who said: I asked Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri about the seal of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), and he said: ""The seal of prophethood on his back was a protruding piece of flesh."
"1063","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace be upon him): There was a man among those who were before you who never did any good deed whatsoever except the declaration of monotheism (Tawheed). When death approached him, he said to his family: ""Look, when I die, burn me until I become ashes, then grind me, then scatter me on a windy day (then scatter half of me on land and half in the sea. By Allah, if Allah has power over me, He will punish me with a punishment the like of which He has not punished anyone in the worlds)."" So when he died, they did that to him. (Then Allah commanded the land to gather what was in it) and there he was, standing in the grip of Allah. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: ""O son of Adam! What made you do what you did?"" He said: ""My Lord, out of fear of You"" — and in another narration: ""Out of awe of You, and You know best."" He said: ""So He forgave him by it, and he never did any good deed whatsoever except the declaration of monotheism."""
"1064","[AI-translation] On the authority of Jundab bin 'Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Among those who came before you was a man who had a wound. He became impatient, took a knife, and cut his hand with it, and the blood did not stop until he died."" Allah, the Exalted, said: ""My servant hastened his soul to Me; I have forbidden Paradise to him."
"1065","[AI-translation] 'As (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""It is an act of disbelief for a man to claim a lineage he does not know, or to deny it, even if it is minor."
"1066","On the authority of Muʿāwiyah ibn Ḥaydah, he said: I said, ""O Prophet of Allah! I did not come to you until I had sworn more oaths than the number of fingers on his two hands that I would not come to you nor follow your religion. And I was a man who understood nothing except what Allah and His Messenger taught me. And I ask you by the Face of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, by what your Lord sent you to us?"" He said: ""With Islam."" I said: ""And what are the signs of Islam?"" He said: ""That you say: 'I have submitted my face to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic,' and you renounce [polytheism], and you establish the prayer, and you give the zakat. Every Muslim is inviolable to another Muslim; they are brothers, supporters of one another. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, does not accept any deed from a polytheist after he has embraced Islam until he separates from the polytheists to the Muslims."""
"1067","[AI-translation] On the authority of 'Abdullah bin Buraydah, from his father, who said: He (peace be upon him and his family) did not see evil omens in anything. When he sent an official, he would ask about his name. If his name pleased him, he would be happy with it, and the joy of that would be seen in his face. And if he disliked the name, his dislike of that would be seen in his face. And when he entered a village, he would ask about its name. If its name pleased him, he would be happy, and the joy of that would be seen in his face. And if he disliked its name, his dislike of that would be seen in his face."
"1068","[AI-translation] On the authority of Ibn 'Abbas, who said: He (peace be upon him and his family) did not seek good omens or evil omens, but a good name pleased him."
"1069","[AI-translation] Darda', they said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What about what we do? Is it a matter that has already been concluded, or is it a matter we are initiating?"" He said: ""Rather, it is a matter that has already been concluded."" They said: ""Then what is the point of action, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""Every person is facilitated for that for which he was created."
"1070","Khalid ibn Dihqan said: We were on the expedition to Constantinople at Dhul-Qiyya when a man from the people of Palestine, from their nobles and best, whom they recognized as such, named Hani' ibn Kulthum ibn Sharik al-Kinani, approached and greeted Abdullah ibn Abi Zakariyya, who used to acknowledge his status. Khalid said to us: So Abdullah ibn Abi Zakariyya narrated to us, saying: I heard Umm al-Darda' say: I heard Abu al-Darda' say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""Every sin, Allah may forgive it, except for one who dies as a polytheist, or a believer who kills a believer intentionally."""
"1071","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him) said: Every bond is severed on the Day of Resurrection except my bond and my lineage."
"1072","[AI-translation] Yamani that he said: I encountered people from the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) saying: Everything is by decree. Tawus said: And I heard Abdullah bin Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Everything is by decree, even incapacity and ability, or ability and incapacity."
"1073","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: Every oath sworn by other than Allah is polytheism."
"1074","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Yazid bin Murthad who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Just as grapes cannot be gathered from thorns, the pious will not be lodged in the dwellings of the wicked. So take whichever path you wish, for whichever path you take, you will arrive at its people."
"1075","[AI-translation] Aswad said: I will not say anything good or evil about a man until I look at what is sealed for him, meaning after something I heard from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family). He was asked: And what did you hear? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: The heart of the son of Adam turns more intensely than a pot when it boils intensely."
"1076","[AI-translation] Darda from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: Everything has a reality, and no servant reaches the reality of faith until he knows that what struck him was not going to miss him, and what missed him was not going to strike him."
"1077","On the authority of a man from Banu Amir who came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) and said: ""May I enter?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the young girl: ""Go out and say to him: Say: 'As-salamu alaykum, may I enter?' For he has not properly sought permission."" He said: ""So I heard it before the young girl came out to me, so I said: 'As-salamu alaykum, may I enter?' He said: 'And upon you, enter.'"" He said: ""So I entered and said: 'With what have you come?' He said: 'I have not come to you except with good. I have come to you that you worship Allah alone, with no partner for Him, and that you abandon the worship of al-Lat and al-Uzza, and that you pray in the night and day five prayers, and that you fast from the year a month, and that you perform Hajj to this House, and that you take from the wealth of your rich and return it to your poor.' Verily Allah knows best. And indeed from knowledge is that which none knows except Allah — five things that none knows except Allah: 'Indeed, Allah has knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and He knows what is in the wombs. And no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die.' Luqman: 34."""
"1078","[AI-translation] Ibn Abbas said: When he (peace be upon him and his family) conquered Mecca, Iblis cried out with a cry, and his soldiers gathered to him. He said: Despair of seeing the nation of Muhammad upon polytheism after this day of yours, but put them to trial in their religion, and spread lamentation among them."
"1079","Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When the night of my Night Journey came, and I woke up in Mecca, I was terrified by my situation and knew that the people would deny me. So I sat aside, grieving. Then the enemy of Allah, Abu Jahl, passed by and came until he sat with him. He said to him, mockingly: 'Was there anything [new]?' The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What is it?' He said: 'I was taken on a night journey tonight.' He said: 'To where?' He said: 'To Bayt al-Maqdis.' He said: 'Then you woke up among us?' He said: 'Yes.' He did not see fit to deny him, fearing that he would refuse to tell the hadith if he called his people to it. He said: 'What do you think, if I call your people, will you tell them what you told me?' The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Come, O people of Banu Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy!' So the gatherings rushed to him, and they came until they sat with them both. He said: 'Tell your people what you told me.' The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'I was taken on a night journey tonight.' They said: 'To where?' He said: 'To Bayt al-Maqdis.' They said: 'Then you woke up among us?' He said: 'Yes.' So some of them clapped their hands, and some placed their hands on their heads in amazement at the lie, they claimed. They said: 'Can you describe the mosque for us, when among the people are those who have traveled to that land and seen the mosque?' The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'So I went to describe it, and I kept describing it until some of the description became confused to me.' He said: 'Then the mosque was brought before me while I was looking, until it was placed near the house of 'Iqal or 'Uqayl, so I described it while looking at it.' He said: 'And there was with this a description I did not memorize.' He said: 'The people said: ""As for the description, by Allah, you have indeed got it right.""'"""
"1080","[AI-translation] Darda, raised to the Prophet: He will not enter the highest degrees who practices soothsaying, or has it practiced for him, or returns from a journey out of taking an evil omen."
"1081","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Hurairah who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: If ten Jews believed in me, no Jew would remain on the surface of the earth but that he would embrace Islam."
"1082","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Hurairah, who said: A man was in need, so he went out to the wilderness. His wife said: O Allah, provide us with what we can knead and what we can bake. The man came, and the bowl was full of dough, and in the oven were sides of roasted meat, and the millstone was grinding. He said: From where is this? She said: From the provision of Allah. He swept what was around the millstone. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Had he left it, it would have turned, or ground until the Day of Resurrection."
"1083","[AI-translation] On the authority of Ibn Umar, raised [to the Prophet]: If you knew the measure of the mercy of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, you would rely upon Him and do no deed, and if you knew the measure of His wrath, nothing would avail you."
"1084","[AI-translation] He said, peace be upon him: Had you said, ""In the name of Allah,"" the angels would have carried you away while the people looked on. He said this to Talha when his fingers were cut off, and he said: ""I feel pain."
"1085","[AI-translation] On the authority of Jabir that a man came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, asking him for food, so he fed him half a wasq of barley. The man continued eating from it, along with his wife and their guest, until he measured it. He came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and he said: Had you not measured it, you would have eaten from it and it would have sufficed for you."
"1086","[AI-translation] Aswad bin Sari', raised: There is no one who loves praise more than Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and no one who grants more excuses than Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"1087","[AI-translation] On the authority of Abu Musa, raised: No one is more patient with an offense He hears than Allah; they attribute a son to Him (and ascribe a partner to Him), yet He grants them well-being (and repels from them) and provides for them (and gives them)."
"1088","[AI-translation] On the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that he saw a man with a brass ring on his arm, so he said to him: What is this? He said: It was prescribed for me for al-Wahinah. He said: Had you died while it was on you, you would have been abandoned to it. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: He is not of us who takes omens or has omens taken for him, or foretells or has foretelling done for him, or practices magic or has magic done for him."
"1089","[AI-translation] On the authority of Ibn Abbas, raised: He is not of us who practices magic or has magic done for him, or foretells or has foretelling done for him, or takes omens or has omens taken for him."
"1090","[AI-translation] On the authority of Anas, he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a state when we are with you, but when we depart from you we are in another state. He said: How are you with your Lord? And Abu Ya'la said: And your Prophet? They said: Allah is our Lord, and in the narration of Abu Ya'la: You are our Prophet, in secret and in public. He said: That is not hypocrisy."
"1091","[AI-translation] Darda', he said: Rain was withheld during the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, so we asked him to pray for rain for us (and he prayed for rain). The Prophet, peace be upon him, went out in the morning, and there he was with a group of people talking, saying: We were given rain by such and such star! The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: Allah does not bestow a blessing upon any people but they become ungrateful for it."
"1092","On the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We were on a military expedition when a man from the Muhajirun kicked a man from the Ansar. The Ansari said: ""O Ansar!"" And the Muhajir said: ""O Muhajirun!"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""What is this call of the Days of Ignorance?"" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, a man from the Muhajirun kicked a man from the Ansar."" He said: ""Leave it, for it is foul."" (Jabir said: The Ansar were more numerous when the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) arrived, then the Muhajirun increased later.) Abdullah ibn Ubayy heard of it and said: ""Have they done so?! By Allah, if we return to Medina, the more honorable will surely expel the more humble from it."" Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Let me strike the neck of this hypocrite."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Leave him, lest people say that Muhammad kills his companions."""
"1093","On the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Sari', who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and went on a military expedition with him. I found myself behind the best of people that day, until they killed the children. And he said once: ""the offspring."" That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), so he said: ""What is the matter with a people that killing has passed them by today until they killed the children?"" A man said: ""O Messenger of Allah! They are only the children of the polytheists."" He said: ""Behold, the best of you are the sons of polytheists."" Then he said: ""Behold, do not kill children. Behold, do not kill children."" He said: ""Every soul is born upon the fitrah until its tongue speaks for it, then its parents make it Jewish or make it Christian."""
"1094","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: There is no one from this Ummah who hears of me, nor a Jew nor a Christian, who does not believe in me except that he will enter the Fire."
"1095","[AI-translation] Mu'adh bin Jabal narrated, raised to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family): There is no soul that dies while testifying that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, with that returning to a convinced heart, except that Allah will forgive it."
"1096","[AI-translation] Abu Razin and 'Abdullah bin 'Umar narrated, raised to the Prophet: The likeness of the believer is the likeness of the date palm; it eats nothing but good and it drops nothing but good."
"1097","Abdur-Rahman bin Jubair bin Nufair narrated from his father who said: We sat with Al-Miqdad bin Al-Aswad one day, and a man passed by him and said: ""Blessed are these two eyes that saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. By Allah, we wished we had seen what you saw and witnessed what you witnessed."" So he became angry, and I was surprised that he said nothing but good. Then he turned to him and said: ""What makes a man wish for a presence that Allah has kept him away from, not knowing how he would have been in it had he witnessed it?! By Allah, there were people who were present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whom Allah threw on their faces in Hellfire; they did not respond to him nor believe him. Do you not praise Allah that He brought you out knowing none but your Lord, believing in what your Prophet brought, having been spared the trial by others? By Allah, Allah sent the Prophet ﷺ in the most severe condition any prophet was sent in, during a period (of ignorance) and Jahiliyyah where they saw no religion better than worshipping idols. He brought a Criterion (Furqan) that separated between truth and falsehood, and separated between a father and his son, until a man would see his father, his son, or his brother as a disbeliever, while Allah had opened the lock of his heart to faith. He knows that if he perishes he will enter the Fire, so his eye finds no rest while he knows his beloved is in the Fire. And this is what Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'And those who say: Our Lord! Grant us from our wives and our offspring the comfort of our eyes' (Al-Furqan: 74)."""
"1098","When Yazid ibn al-Muhallab was appointed governor of Khurasan, he said: ""Direct me to a man who is complete in the qualities of goodness."" He was directed to Abu Burdah ibn Abu Musa al-Ash'ari. When he came to him, he saw a man of surpassing appearance; and when he spoke with him, he found his inner reality better than his outward appearance. He said: ""I have appointed you over such-and-such of my affairs."" He sought exemption, but he refused to exempt him. He said: ""O Commander! Shall I not inform you of something my father narrated to me, that he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" He said: ""Bring it forth."" He said: ""He heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'Whoever assumes a position of authority while knowing that he is not fit for that position, let him take his seat in the Fire.'"" He said: ""And I bear witness, O Commander, that I am not fit for what you have called me to."" Yazid said to him: ""You have only incited me against yourself and increased my desire for you. Go forth to your covenant, for I will not exempt you."" Then he went out (the original text says: 'then he went out,' but perhaps the correct reading is: 'he went out, then') and remained in it as long as Allah willed. Then he sought permission to return to him, and he granted him permission. He said: ""O Commander! Shall I not narrate to you something my father narrated to me, that he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?"" He said: ""Bring it forth."" He said: ""Cursed is he who asks by the Face of Allah, and cursed is he who is asked by the Face of Allah and then refuses his petitioner what he did not ask for out of arrogance."" He said: ""And I ask you by the Face of Allah, O Commander, that you exempt me from your work."" So he exempted him."
"1099","[AI-translation] Jabir bin 'Abdullah narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him): Whoever goes to a soothsayer and believes what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad."
"1100","[AI-translation] Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Will we be held accountable for what we did in the period of ignorance?"" He said: ""Whoever does good in Islam will not be held accountable for what he did in the period of ignorance, and whoever does evil in Islam will be held accountable for the first and the last."
"1101","[AI-translation] Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Whoever does good in what remains [of his life] will be forgiven for what has passed, and whoever does evil in what remains will be held accountable for what has passed and what remains."
"1102","[AI-translation] Bahili said: I was under the riding animal of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and he spoke good words, and among what he said was: ""Whoever embraces Islam from the People of the two Books, for him is his reward twice, and for him is the like of what is for us, and upon him is the like of what is upon us. And whoever embraces Islam from the polytheists, for him is his reward, and for him is the like of what is for us, and upon him is the like of what is upon us."
"1103","[AI-translation] Ibn 'Abbas narrated, raised to the Prophet: Whoever acquires knowledge from the stars has acquired a branch of magic."
"1104","[AI-translation] Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated, raised to the Prophet: Whoever calls to guidance will have a reward like the rewards of those who follow him, without that diminishing anything from their rewards. And whoever calls to misguidance will have a sin upon him like the sins of those who follow him, without that diminishing anything from their sins."
"1105","[AI-translation] Ibn 'Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Whoever sees an afflicted person and says: ""Praise be to Allah who has spared me what He has afflicted you with, and preferred me over many of His creations, a distinct preference,"" that trial will not befall him."
"1106","[AI-translation] Abu Hurairah narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: Whoever is pleased to find the taste of faith, let him love a person, loving him not except for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"1107","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin 'Amr, raised to the Prophet: Whoever lets the people hear of his deeds, Allah will expose him to the hearing of His creation on the Day of Resurrection, and He will humiliate him and belittle him."
"1108","[AI-translation] From 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, raised to the Prophet: Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah will enter Paradise."
"1109","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Whoever prays our prayer, faces our Qiblah, and eats our slaughtered meat, he is the Muslim who has the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger. So do not violate the protection of Allah regarding him."
"1110","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin 'Abdullah, raised to the Prophet: Whoever says: ""There is no god but Allah"" sincerely will enter Paradise."
"1111","[AI-translation] Juhani, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Whoever meets Allah without associating anything with Him, and is not tainted by unlawful blood, will enter Paradise."
"1112","[AI-translation] From Mu'adh bin Jabal, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: Whoever meets Allah without associating anything with Him, prays the five prayers, and fasts Ramadan, will be forgiven. I said: ""Shall I not give them the glad tidings, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""Leave them to perform deeds."
"1113","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: Whoever does not supplicate to Allah, Glorified be He, He becomes angry with him."
"1114","[AI-translation] From Ibn Mas'ud, raised to the Prophet: Whoever dies associating anything with Allah will enter the Fire."
"1115","[AI-translation] Ashja'i, from his father (Tariq bin Ashyam), raised to the Prophet: Whoever declares the oneness of Allah, the Most High, and disbelieves in what is worshipped besides Him, his wealth and blood are inviolable, and his reckoning is upon Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"1116","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, he said: The believer is the mirror of the believer, and the believer is the brother of the believer; he protects him from loss and guards him from behind."
"1117","[AI-translation] From Sahl ibn Sa'd, marfu': The believer from the people of faith is like the head to the body. The believer feels pain for what afflicts the people of faith, just as the head feels pain for what afflicts the body."
"1118","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim. He does not wrong him nor surrender him. Whoever is in the need of his brother, Allah is in his need. And whoever relieves a Muslim of a distress, Allah relieves him of a distress from the distresses of the Day of Resurrection. And whoever shields a Muslim, Allah shields him on the Day of Resurrection."
"1119","[AI-translation] Nu'man ibn Bashir, may Allah be pleased with him, marfu': The Muslims are like one man; if his eye complains, his whole body complains, and if his head complains, his whole body complains."
"1120","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said to Abu Dharr: Which knot of faith—I think he said: is the firmest? He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Loyalty in Allah, enmity in Allah, love in Allah, and hatred in Allah."
"1121","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said to Abu Dharr: Which knot of faith—I think he said: is the firmest? He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Loyalty in Allah, enmity in Allah, love in Allah, and hatred in Allah."
"1122","[AI-translation] From Ibn Zurara, from his father, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, he said: It was revealed concerning a people from my Ummah at the end of time who will deny the decree of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Meaning His saying: ""Taste the touch of Saqar"" (48) ""Indeed, all things We created with decree"" (49) (Al-Qamar)."
"1123","Aban ibn Uthman said: Zayd ibn Thabit left Marwan's presence around midday. We said: ""He must have sent for him only to ask him about something."" So I went to him and asked him. He said: ""Yes, he asked us about things I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'May Allah brighten a person who hears a hadith from us, preserves it, and conveys it to others. For perhaps a carrier of knowledge is not a scholar, and perhaps a carrier of knowledge conveys it to one who is more knowledgeable than him. Three things concerning which the heart of a Muslim never harbors rancor: sincerity of action for Allah, sincere advice to those in authority, and adherence to the community. For their supplication encompasses them from behind. Whoever makes the Hereafter his concern, Allah will gather his affairs, place richness in his heart, and the world will come to him submissive. And whoever makes the world his intention, Allah will scatter his affairs, place poverty between his eyes, and nothing of the world will come to him except what was decreed for him.'"""
"1124","[AI-translation] Zuraqi, that Asma' bint 'Umays said: O Messenger of Allah! The evil eye quickly afflicts the children of Ja'far, should I seek ruqyah for them? He said: Yes, for if there were anything that could precede the decree, the evil eye would precede it."
"1125","On the authority of Khuraym ibn Fatik al-Asadi, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""People are of four types, and deeds are of six types. As for people: 1) One who is given abundance in this world and the Hereafter; 2) One who is given abundance in this world but is straitened in the Hereafter; 3) One who is straitened in this world but is given abundance in the Hereafter; 4) One who is wretched in this world and the Hereafter. As for deeds: 1 and 2) Two that necessitate (reward or punishment); 3 and 4) Like for like; 5) Tenfold; 6) Seven hundredfold. 1 and 2) The two that necessitate: Whoever dies as a Muslim believer, associating nothing with Allah, Paradise becomes obligatory for him; and whoever dies as a disbeliever, Hellfire becomes obligatory for him. 3 and 4) Whoever intends a good deed but does not perform it, and Allah knows that he has felt it in his heart and strove for it, it is recorded for him as a good deed; and whoever intends an evil deed, it is not recorded against him, and if he performs it, it is recorded as one, not multiplied against him. 5) Whoever performs a good deed, it is for him ten times its like. 6) Whoever spends a expenditure in the way of Allah, it is for him seven hundredfold."""
"1126","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, regarding the two handfuls: These are for this, and these are for this."
"1127","Ibn Abbas narrated: A man from Banu Amir came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), and he was a physician and healer. He said: ""O Muhammad! You say things; would you like me to treat you?"" The Messenger of Allah invited him to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, then said: ""Would you like me to show you a sign?"" There were palm trees and a tree nearby. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) called a cluster of dates from it, and it came to him, prostrating and raising its head until it reached him, and it stood before him. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to it: ""Return to your place,"" so it returned to its place. The Amiri man said: ""By Allah! I will never belie you in any statement ever again."" Then he said: ""O family of Banu Sa'sa'ah! By Allah! I will never belie him in anything he says ever again."""
"1128","[AI-translation] From Abu Salih, he said: I heard Abu al-Darda' being asked about: ""Those who believe and are God-fearing"" (63) ""For them are glad tidings in the worldly life"" (Yunus). He said: No one has asked me since I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and he said: No one has asked me about it before you: It is the righteous dream which a servant sees or is shown to him."
"1129","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, marfu': By the One in Whose hand is my soul, no man from this Ummah, nor a Jew, nor a Christian hears of me and then does not believe in me, except that he will be from the people of the Fire."
"1130","On the authority of Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, from his father, who said: While we were walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), he heard a man in the valley saying: ""I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah."" So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""And I bear witness, and I bear witness that no one bears witness to it except that he is absolved from polytheism."" Meaning the two testimonies. The wording is from An-Nasa'i. And At-Tabarani added at its beginning: When he heard the people saying: ""Which deed is best, O Messenger of Allah?"" So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Faith in Allah and His Messenger, jihad in the path of Allah, and an accepted Hajj."" Then he heard... the hadith."
"1131","[AI-translation] From Umm Salamah, she said: I said to the Prophet, peace be upon him: Hisham bin Al-Mughirah used to maintain ties of kinship, honor the guest, free the captive, and feed the food. Had he reached Islam, would that have benefited him? He said: No. He used to give for the sake of the world and its mention, and its praise, and he never said a single day: My Lord, forgive me my sin on the Day of Judgment."
"1132","[AI-translation] Samit who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and said: O Prophet of Allah! Which deed is best? He said: Faith in Allah, attestation to Him, and jihad in His cause. He said: I want something easier than that, O Messenger of Allah! He said: Forbearance and patience. He said: I want something easier than that, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do not suspect Allah, Blessed and Exalted, in anything He decrees for you."
"1133","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Do not curse time, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am time. The days and the nights are Mine; I renew them and wear them out, and I bring kings after kings."
"1134","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin 'Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: Do not consider provision slow in coming, for no servant will die until he reaches the last of his provision that is for him. So be moderate in seeking, taking the lawful and leaving the unlawful."
"1135","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Do not marvel at the deed of anyone until you see what he is sealed with, for a person may work for a period of his life or a portion of his life with a righteous deed; were he to die upon it, he would enter Paradise, then he changes and does an evil deed. And a servant may work for a period of his life with an evil deed; were he to die upon it, he would enter the Fire, then he changes and does a righteous deed. And when Allah intends good for a servant, He employs him before his death, granting him success to do a righteous deed, then takes him in that state."
"1136","[AI-translation] Sa'ib bin Yazid, the nephew of Nimr, marfu'an: There is no contagion, no Safar, and no Hāmah."
"1137","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, marfu'an: There is no contagion, no evil omen, and I love good optimism."
"1138","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar, marfu'an: There is no contagion and no evil omen, and evil omens are only in three things: the woman, the horse, and the house."
"1139","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, marfu'an: There is no contagion, no evil omen, and the evil eye is true."
"1140","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu'an: There is no contagion, no evil omen, no Safar, and no Hāmah. A Bedouin said: What is the matter with camels that are in the sand like gazelles, and a mangy camel mixes with them and makes them mangy? He said: So who infected the first?"
"1141","[AI-translation] From Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, marfu'an: ""There is no contagion, no evil omen, and no ghoul."
"1142","[AI-translation] Musayyab who said: ""I asked Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas about the evil omen? He scolded me and said: 'Who told you?!' I disliked telling him who told me. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: 'There is no contagion, no evil omen, and no hama. If there were to be an evil omen in anything, it would be in the horse, the woman, and the house. And if you hear of a plague in a land, do not go down into it, and if it occurs in a land while you are in it, do not flee from it.'"
"1143","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, marfu'an: ""There is no contagion, no evil omen, no hama, and no Safar, and flee from the leper as you flee from a lion."
"1144","[AI-translation] From Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, marfu'an: ""There is no contagion and no evil omen, and I like a good omen, the good word."
"1145","[AI-translation] Zinad who said: ""Men of approval and contentment from among the children of the Companions and the early people narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: 'There is no contagion, no hama, and no Safar, and avoid the leper as one avoids a lion.'"
"1146","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""We do not know anything better than a hundred like it, except the believing man."
"1147","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik, marfu'an: ""None of you believes until he loves for his brother what he loves for himself (of good). ( )"
"1148","[AI-translation] From Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah, marfu'an: ""A servant does not believe until he believes in divine decree, its good and its evil, until he knows that what struck him was not going to miss him, and that what missed him was not going to strike him."
"1149","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah, she said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Ibn Jad'an was in the Jahiliyyah maintaining ties of kinship and feeding the poor, so will that avail him?"" He said: ""No, O 'A'ishah! He never said a day: 'My Lord, forgive me my sin on the Day of Recompense.'"
"1150","[AI-translation] Darda', may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, he said: ""A servant does not attain the reality of faith until he knows that what struck him was not going to miss him, and that what missed him was not going to strike him."
"1151","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet said: Faith and disbelief do not combine in a man's heart, nor do lying and truthfulness combine together, nor do treachery and trustworthiness combine together."
"1152","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas bin Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, entered upon a young man while he was dying and said: ""How do you find yourself?"" He said: ""I hope for Allah, O Messenger of Allah, and I fear my sins."" So the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""These two - meaning fear and hope - do not combine in the heart of a servant in such a situation - meaning at the point of death - except that Allah gives him what he hopes for and secures him from what he fears."
"1153","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Rayhanah that the Prophet said: No part of arrogance will enter Paradise. A man said: ""O Prophet of Allah! I love to beautify myself with the end of my whip and the strap of my sandal."" The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Indeed, that is not arrogance. Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is Beautiful and loves beauty. Indeed, arrogance is rejecting the truth and belittling people."
"1154","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The affairs of this Ummah will continue to be in harmony, or nearly so, as long as they do not speak about the children and predestination."
"1155","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin Samurah that the Prophet said: The religion will remain established until the Hour is established, or until there are over you twelve caliphs, all of them from Quraysh."
"1156","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas bin Malik that the Prophet said: People will continue to ask, saying, ""What is this? What is this?"" until they say, ""Allah created the people, so who created Allah?"" At that point, they will go astray."
"1157","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin Samurah: This religion will remain established, with a group of Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour is established."
"1158","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah that the Prophet said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer, nor does the drinker drink alcohol while he is a believer, nor does the thief steal while he is a believer, nor does the plunderer plunder something while the people raise their eyes to him while he is a believer."
"1159","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Umar that the Prophet said: A believer is not stung from the same hole twice."
"1160","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah that the Prophet said: Satan comes to one of you and says, ""Who created this? Who created this? Who created this?"" until he says, ""Who created your Lord?"" When it reaches that, let him seek refuge in Allah and stop."
"1161","[AI-translation] From Ubayd Allah ibn Miqsam: that he looked at Abdullah ibn Umar as he related from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, takes His heavens and earths in His hands and says: ""I am Allah."" And he clenched his fingers and spread them: ""I am the King."" (And the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, swayed to his right and to his left) until I looked at the pulpit moving from its lower part, until I said: ""Is he falling with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him?"
"1162","[AI-translation] Hubrani, he said: Abu Umamah al-Bahili took my hand and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, took my hand and said: ""O Abu Umamah, indeed among the believers are those whose hearts soften towards me."
"1163","[AI-translation] From Abdullah ibn Amr, the Prophet, peace be upon him, said to Abu Bakr: ""O Abu Bakr, if Allah had willed not to be disobeyed, He would not have created Iblis."
"1164","[AI-translation] From Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, delivered a sermon to us in the middle of the days of Tashriq, the Farewell Sermon, and he said: ""O people, indeed your Lord is one and your father is one. Indeed, there is no superiority of an Arab over a non-Arab, nor a non-Arab over an Arab, nor a red over a black, nor a black over a red, except by piety. Indeed, the most noble of you in the sight of Allah is the most pious of you. Have I not conveyed?"" They said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Then let the witness convey to the absent."
"1165","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah, he said: When this verse was revealed — ""And warn your closest kindred"" (Qur'an 26:214) — the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) called the Quraysh, so they gathered. He addressed them generally and specifically, saying: ""O sons of Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy! Save yourselves from the Fire! O sons of Murrah ibn Ka'b! Save yourselves from the Fire! O sons of 'Abd Shams! Save yourselves from the Fire! O sons of 'Abd Manaf! Save yourselves from the Fire! O sons of 'Abd al-Muttalib! Save yourselves from the Fire! O Fatimah (daughter of Muhammad)! Save yourself from the Fire! For I possess no power for you against Allah whatsoever, except that you have kinship ties which I will maintain with their due rights."""
"1166","[AI-translation] From Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said to me: ""O Abdullah ibn Amr! You fast perpetually and stand the night in prayer, and if you do that, the eye will become weary and the soul worn out—and in a narration: and the self will become fatigued. Let him not fast who fasts forever; fasting three days of the month is the fasting of the entire month."" I said: ""I am able to do more than that."" He said: ""Then fast the fast of Dawud; he used to fast one day and break the fast the next, and he did not flee when he met (the enemy)."
"1167","[AI-translation] From Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""A man will come on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds which he thinks will save him, but a man will keep coming forward whom he had oppressed, so his good deeds will be taken and given to the oppressed until no good deed remains for him. Then someone whom he had oppressed will come, and nothing remains of his good deeds, so the bad deeds of the oppressed will be taken and placed upon his bad deeds."
"1168","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him, said: ""Allah, Blessed and Exalted, looks upon His creation on the night of the middle of Sha'ban, and He forgives all of His creation except for an idolater or one who harbors hatred."
"1169","[AI-translation] From Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Some people of Tawhid will be punished in the Fire until they become charcoal therein, then the mercy of Allah will reach them, and they will be brought out and cast at the gates of Paradise."" He said: ""The people of Paradise will sprinkle water upon them, and they will sprout as the debris sprouts in the floodwater, and then they will enter Paradise."
"1170","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah who said: A man came and said: ""I saw as if my head was struck and I saw it rolling."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Satan approaches one of you and frightens him, then he goes about informing the people."
"1171","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: ""I sought a loan from My servant and he did not lend to Me, and My servant insults Me while he does not know—and in a narration: and he is not entitled to insult Me. He says: 'O Dhahr! O Dhahr!' three times, and I am Ad-Dahr."
"1172","[AI-translation] Abu Dharr reported: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: ""Whoever does a good deed will have ten times its like or more, and whoever does an evil deed, its recompense is its like or I will forgive. Whoever commits a sin the fill of the earth, then meets Me not associating anything with Me, I will make for him its like in forgiveness. Whoever draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him an arm's length; and whoever draws near to Me an arm's length, I draw near to him a fathom; and whoever comes to Me walking, I come to him running."
"1173","[AI-translation] Abu Hurairah reported: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The Right Hand of Allah is full; no expenditure diminishes it, pouring out night and day. Have you seen what He has spent since He created the heavens and the earth? Indeed, it has not diminished what is in His right Hand."" He said: ""And His Throne is upon the water, and in His other Hand is the grasp; He raises and lowers."
"1174","[AI-translation] Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, reported: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, say: ""People will soon question one another until one of them says: 'This is Allah who created the creation, so who created Allah, Mighty and Majestic?' When they say that, say: 'Allah is One, Allah is the Eternal Refuge, He neither begets nor is born, nor is there to Him any equivalent' [Al-Ikhlas], then let one of you spit to his left three times, and seek refuge in Allah from the Shaytan."
